dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/

# secrets — never commit (a bare ".env" does NOT match ".env.bak", ".env.local", ...)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
*.pem
*.p12
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
secrets.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json
_*.log

# Demo residue. examples/01_basics.py persists to a RELATIVE path, and the suite used to run the examples
# with cwd=<repo>, so every run appended to this file -- 85 runs of the same demo, 340 records, 337 of them
# superseded, COMMITTED. A fresh clone running our flagship "a correction stays corrected" example printed
# a wall of duplicates before reaching the one active line. The file is generated; it does not belong here.
memory.json
# Same class, the DEFAULT path rather than the demo's: a bare `Inspeximus()` in any probe or doctest
# persists to ./inspeximus_memory.json (+ its tombstone sidecar) in whatever cwd it ran from. Two empty
# ones were sitting untracked in the root when 1.87.0 was cut. Generated state must not be committable.
inspeximus_memory.json
inspeximus_memory.json.tombstones.json

# Benchmark inputs and derived artifacts. THIRD-PARTY DATA IS NOT OURS TO SHIP, and a derived cache is
# not evidence -- both were once committed here by accident and turned a benchmark PR into a 69,000-line
# diff, which is unreviewable and therefore unreviewed. What belongs in git is the config, the harness,
# and the RESULT: benchmarks/locomo/config.json pins the dataset's sha256 so anyone can verify they hold
# the same file, and run.py resolves it via --data / $INSPEXIMUS_LOCOMO_PATH / this ignored directory.
benchmarks/locomo/data/
benchmarks/locomo/.cache/
# Run artifacts. `<subset>.json` is the committed baseline; `<subset>.latest.json` is whatever the last
# re-run produced and exists only to be diffed against it.
benchmarks/locomo/results/*.latest.json
